Here is a very minor problem that I hope will be addressed in latex 3,
if it hasn't already been.  Since I (and probably many others) use
a 20pt style for transparencies (in slitex, most of my favourite
macros are unavailable, for want of fonts), I have made a 20pt style
file.  In the process, I discovered that article.sty is hardwired to
accept fontsizes only in the form 1x.  I could, of course, have called
it 19, but the change was totally trivial.  Unfortunately, the resultant
file is no longer article.sty, which makes it nonportable.  Since I feel
that in general LL did a remarkable job in designing latex, I will keep
to myself the adjective I use to describe this design decision, but I
hope the designers of latex 3 will do better here.

Michael Barr

